    feat(install): ship shared Claude Code user setup
    
    `superclaude install` and `update` now also install:
    - all IronFlow document/workflow templates (IronFlow copies are newer);
    - the rules those templates read, under ~/.claude/rules/{core,contextual,prompts},
      listed by exact path in claudeMdExcludes so Claude Code never auto-loads
      them; template and rule references now point at ~/.claude/rules/;
    - the Pragmatic output style and its SubagentStart hook;
    - settings defaults (output style, model, effort, thinking, behavior flags,
      env, per-model effort, plugins, marketplaces), filled only where the user
      has not set a value;
    - Orca's computer-use, orca-cli and orchestration skills via the Orca CLI,
      and the default plugins via the claude CLI, within a shared 30-second
      network budget and never failing the install.
    
    `update` now also refreshes templates. Makefile sync checks include .js hooks.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>

